<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GonilInterface - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gonilinterface/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gonilinterface/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 176</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_176/</link><pubDate>Wed, 05 Feb 2025 00:45:26 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_176/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code? Why?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;&#10;type People interface {&#10; Show()&#10;}&#10;&#10;type Student struct{}&#10;&#10;func (stu *Student) Show() {&#10;&#10;}&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10;&#10; var s *Student&#10; if s == nil {&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;s is nil&amp;#34;)&#10; } else {&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;s is not nil&amp;#34;)&#10; }&#10; var p People = s&#10; if p == nil {&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;p is nil&amp;#34;)&#10; } else {&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;p is not nil&amp;#34;)&#10; }&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;s is nil&#10;p is not nil&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Remember, an interface type value is &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt; if and only if both its dynamic value and dynamic type are &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 140</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_140/</link><pubDate>Tue, 24 Dec 2024 23:28:20 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_140/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() { &#10; var i interface{}&#10; if i == nil {&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;nil&amp;#34;)&#10; return&#10; }&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;not nil&amp;#34;)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. nil&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. not nil&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;A &lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/rtD7YmJZxp1" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Simply put, an interface variable has two values: one is its type, and the other is its value.&#10;For an &lt;code&gt;if&lt;/code&gt; interface, the &lt;code&gt;live() == nil&lt;/code&gt; condition is true only when both the value and the type are zero values.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 136</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_136/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Dec 2024 22:34:36 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_136/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code compile?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import (&#10; &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;)&#10;&#10;type worker interface {&#10; work()&#10;}&#10;&#10;type person struct {&#10; name string&#10; worker&#10;}&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; var w worker = person{}&#10; fmt.Println(w)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A: Yes;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B: No;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C: Don&amp;rsquo;t know&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Answer: A &lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/RSSWTD3otlJ" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 class="heading-element" id="01"&gt;&lt;span&gt;01&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#01" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We all know Go doesn&amp;rsquo;t have inheritance, but it can simulate some inheritance features through embedded types. It&amp;rsquo;s important to remember that interfaces are also types, and naturally, they can be used as embedded types. If the &lt;code&gt;person&lt;/code&gt; struct in the problem were changed to:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>